;THE SEQUENCE DATABASE FOR CHAINS A,C RESIDUES 1-107 IS
CAH04481.2, AND FOR CHAINS B,D RESIDUES 1-113 IS CAH04480.1.
RESIDUE NUMBERING OF ANTIBODY VARIABLE REGIONS
FOLLOWS THE KABAT CONVENTION (E.A. KABAT, T.T. WU, H.M.
PERRY, K.S. GOTTESMAN, C. FOELLER. SEQUENCES OF PROTEINS OF
IMMUNOLOGICAL INTEREST, 5TH ED. (1991). NIH PUBLICATION NO.
91-3242, NATIONAL INSTITUTES OF HEALTH, BETHESDA, MD).
DISCREPANCIES BETWEEN THE DATABASE SEQUENCE CAH04481.2 AND
THIS PDB ENTRY OCCUR AT POSITIONS ASP 1, ILE 2, ALA 7, ALA 8,
AND PHE 9 (CHAINS A,C), AND BETWEEN DATABASE SEQUENCE
CAH04480.1 AND THIS ENTRY AT POSITION VAL 4 (CHAINS B,D).
THESE N-TERMINAL SEQUENCE DISCREPANCIES ARE DUE TO THE PRIMERS
USED FOR NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE DETERMINATION.
;
